//? Title: CycleGAN: Disjoint Domains and One Joint Generator Snapshot
//? Subtitle: An explicit native unpaired training loop, preserved weak results and known-mapping diagnostics
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Two independent grayscale domains are drawn from disjoint halves of each MNIST
class. Domain B is rotated and inverted, but that known mapping is used only for
diagnostics. Two independent two-skip U-Nets and two unconditional patch critics
share a least-squares adversarial, cycle-L1 and identity-L1 objective. The complete
C++ program keeps every critic write and the jointly captured generator vectors
visible. It reproduces all original outputs and the source control showing that
recomputing the second G gradient after the first write changes the method.
Three fixed epochs leave weak translations, cycle L1 about.46/.47 and known-map
MSE about.229/.210. Fitting-only domain means provide an additional reference.
Correct cycle arithmetic and capture order do not establish a learned mapping.
)
\toc

> Reuse each generator in both a translation and a round trip

[Zhu, Park, Isola and Efros, Unpaired Image-to-Image Translation using
Cycle-Consistent Adversarial Networks (ICCV2017)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.10593)
combines adversarial distribution matching with cycle consistency. This source
uses tiny28x28 U-Nets,18x18 nominal patch receptive fields and no image buffer,
normalization or dropout. It does not reproduce the paper's full architecture
or evaluation. All4102 values in32 tensors belong to four independent stores:
G_ab1390,G_ba1390,D_a661,D_b661. G maps read their source alone; no opposite-domain
target, label, noise or known rotation enters their inputs or the objective.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cycle_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(48, 1500);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle a;
  a.width     = 7.3;
  a.height    = 4.8;
  a.font_size = 42;
  d.node("a", {-18, 7}, "A source a\nIndependent rows", a)
      .node("ab", {-9, 7}, "G_ab (group0)\nShared weights", a)
      .node("fb", {0, 7}, "fake_b\nG_ab(a)", a)
      .node("ba2", {9, 7}, "G_ba (group1)\nSame G_ba below", a)
      .node("ca", {18, 7}, "cycle_a\nCompare with a", a)
      .node("b", {-18, -7}, "B source b\nDisjoint IDs", a)
      .node("ba", {-9, -7}, "G_ba (group1)\nShared weights", a)
      .node("fa", {0, -7}, "fake_a\nG_ba(b)", a)
      .node("ab2", {9, -7}, "G_ab (group0)\nSame G_ab above", a)
      .node("cb", {18, -7}, "cycle_b\nCompare with b", a)
      .edge("a", "ab")
      .edge("ab", "fb")
      .edge("fb", "ba2")
      .edge("ba2", "ca")
      .edge("b", "ba")
      .edge("ba", "fa")
      .edge("fa", "ab2")
      .edge("ab2", "cb")
      .save_svg("build/cycle_method.svg");
}
