\alttext(An executed unconditional critic trace reduces28x28 grayscale input to7x7 raw patch scores, retaining all six learned tensors.)

> Prepare the real disjoint image domains through native APIs

`prepare_example_data("mnist-assets",...)` and `LoadSaliency` provide the original
1000/200/200 fitting/validation/test rows, source IDs, balanced labels and exact
byte normalization. `SplitCycleDomains` makes500/500 fitting A/B rows and100/100
in each held-out pool. The first half of every digit supplies original A and the
second half supplies rotated/inverted B. Their source IDs are disjoint across
domains and checked original pools. The preview selects each class through
original-ID metadata; those labels remain outside the model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cycle_domains.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
std::vector<std::int64_t> BalancedRows(const n::Tensor& ids, const m::SaliencyData& pool) {
  std::map<std::int64_t, std::int64_t> label;
  auto                                 source = pool.source.to_vector<std::int64_t>(),
       labels = pool.labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>(), selected = ids.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < source.size(); ++i)
    label.emplace(source[i], labels[i]);
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    bool found = false;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < selected.size(); ++i)
      if (label.at(selected[i]) == c) {
        rows.push_back(i);
        found = true;
        break;
      }
    if (!found)
      throw std::runtime_error("all ten diagnostic classes");
  }
  return rows;
}
int main() {
  auto path = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency";
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", path.parent_path());
  auto pools = m::LoadSaliency(path);
  auto d     = m::SplitCycleDomains(pools[0].images, pools[0].labels, pools[0].source);
  auto ar = BalancedRows(d.ids_a, pools[0]), br = BalancedRows(d.ids_b, pools[0]);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    panels.push_back(n::take_rows(d.a, {ar[c]}));
    panels.push_back(n::take_rows(d.b, {br[c]}));
  }
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(panels, 0), "build/cycle_domains.png", 2, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/cycle_domains.png)
// result_end
\caption(Rows0 through9 show different fitting observations from the two domains, A then B. The two panels in a row are display choices from disjoint sources, not supervised training pairs.)
\alttext(Ten real digit classes show original-domain and rotated/inverted-domain fitting examples drawn from different original source IDs.)

> Keep the full critic and joint-generator schedule visible

Independent batch orders use seeds6233/6247. Every epoch visits all500 rows in
each fitting domain, with15 full32-row batches and one retained20-row batch.
Three fixed epochs give48 steps per group and192 writes. Four independent Adam
states use.0002,beta1=.5,beta2=.999,epsilon1e-8. Validation is recorded without
selecting a checkpoint; the final epoch is fixed before looking at test results.
An optional edited init path imports all32 checkpoint tensors; the preserved run
uses the stated native seeds.

For each batch D_a and D_b take their own fresh captures and selected writes.
A fresh common G forward through both updated critics then supplies both generator
vectors before either write. The visible capture helper performs exactly one
forward for every requested group set. G_ab and G_ba apply those saved vectors.
The first-step wrong control recomputes G_ba after G_ab and measures the changed
gradient, without applying it. Every phase verifies that other stores stay bit
exact. The API has no capture, optimizer, hidden no-grad, known target mapping or
mutable normalization state. It permits unequal positive domain row counts;
this original schedule deliberately uses equal independent batch sizes.

All ten original archives/2467653 values, both galleries, history,batch records and
non-timing metrics are preserved. The program additionally retains347 phase/probe
archives/3988406 values, including each critic capture, the joint G capture, every
post-write store, epoch outputs and wrong-gradient control. Known mapping targets
are created only after the fixed final checkpoint, for diagnostics. Restoration
initializes independent stores(seed1/2/3/4) and verifies all4102 values exactly.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cycle_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <cmath>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>

namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace n  = nn;
namespace m  = nn::models;
using Arrays = std::map<std::string, nn::Tensor>;
using nn::Tensor;

namespace {
void Require(bool condition, const std::string& message) {
  if (!condition)
    throw std::runtime_error(message);
}
void SaveArrays(const std::string& path, const Arrays& a) {
  nn::save_npz(path, nn::NamedTensors(a.begin(), a.end()));
}
bool Equal(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  return nn::equal_bits(a, b);
}
bool Equal(const Arrays& a, const Arrays& b) {
  if (a.size() != b.size())
    return false;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
    if (!b.count(key) || !Equal(value, b.at(key)))
      return false;
  return true;
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  return nn::max(nn::abs(nn::cast(a, nn::DType::Float64) - nn::cast(b, nn::DType::Float64))).item();
}
Arrays Fields(const m::CycleGanOutput& o) {
  return {
      {"fake_a", o.fake_a},
      {"fake_b", o.fake_b},
      {"cycle_a", o.cycle_a},
      {"cycle_b", o.cycle_b},
      {"identity_a", o.identity_a},
      {"identity_b", o.identity_b},
      {"real_a_score", o.real_a_score},
      {"real_b_score", o.real_b_score},
      {"fake_a_score", o.fake_a_score},
      {"fake_b_score", o.fake_b_score},
      {"g_loss", o.g_loss},
      {"d_a_loss", o.d_a_loss},
      {"d_b_loss", o.d_b_loss},
      {"adversarial_a", o.adversarial_a},
      {"adversarial_b", o.adversarial_b},
      {"cycle_loss_a", o.cycle_loss_a},
      {"cycle_loss_b", o.cycle_loss_b},
      {"identity_loss_a", o.identity_loss_a},
      {"identity_loss_b", o.identity_loss_b}};
}
double Value(const Arrays& a, const std::string& key) {
  return a.at(key).item();
}
Tensor Flat784(const Tensor& x) {
  return nn::reshape(x, {-1, 784});
}
Tensor Rows(const Tensor& x, const std::vector<std::int64_t>& rows) {
  return nn::take_rows(x, rows);
}
void RequireOnlyOwnersChanged(
    const Arrays&                   before,
    const Arrays&                   after,
    const std::vector<std::string>& prefixes,
    const std::string&              message,
    bool                            require_change) {
  bool changed = false;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : before) {
    bool selected = false;
    for (const auto& prefix : prefixes)
      selected |= key.starts_with(prefix);
    if (!Equal(value, after.at(key))) {
      Require(selected, message);
      changed = true;
    }
  }
  if (require_change)
    Require(changed, message + " changed selected values");
}
void Mosaic(const std::filesystem::path& path, const Tensor& images, std::int64_t columns) {
  nn::save_image_grid(
      nn::reshape(images, {-1, 28, 28, 1}), path.string(), columns, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
}
} // namespace
int main() {
  const auto data = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency";
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", data.parent_path());
  const std::filesystem::path root   = "build/cycle_gan";
  const int                   epochs = 3;
  const std::string           init;

  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  const auto                   pools = m::LoadSaliency(data);
  std::vector<m::CycleDomains> domains;
  Arrays                       records;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    domains.push_back(m::SplitCycleDomains(pools[k].images, pools[k].labels, pools[k].source));
    const std::string name = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    records.emplace(name + "_a", domains.back().a);
    records.emplace(name + "_b", domains.back().b);
    records.emplace(name + "_ids_a", domains.back().ids_a);
    records.emplace(name + "_ids_b", domains.back().ids_b);
  }
  SaveArrays((root / "data.npz").string(), records);
  n::ParameterStore               g_ab(6203), g_ba(6211), d_a(6217), d_b(6221);
  std::vector<n::ParameterStore*> stores{&g_ab, &g_ba, &d_a, &d_b};
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    auto           zero = n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1});
    m::Pix2PixGenerate(g_ab, zero);
    m::Pix2PixGenerate(g_ba, zero);
    m::CycleGanDiscriminate(d_a, zero);
    m::CycleGanDiscriminate(d_b, zero);
  }
  auto forward = [&](const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
    return m::CycleGan(g_ab, g_ba, d_a, d_b, a, b);
  };
  auto snapshot = [&]() {
    Arrays out;
    for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k)
      for (const auto& name : stores[k]->names())
        out.emplace(std::to_string(k) + "/" + name, stores[k]->at(name).detach().clone());
    return out;
  };
  auto evaluate = [&](const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    return Fields(forward(a, b));
  };
  auto capture = [&](const std::vector<int>& groups, const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
    // ONE forward for all requested groups; no write occurs inside capture.
    const auto     out = forward(a, b);
    Arrays         result;
    n::GradOptions keep;
    keep.retain_graph = true;
    for (int k : groups) {
      auto gradient = n::grad(
          k < 2    ? out.g_loss
          : k == 2 ? out.d_a_loss
                   : out.d_b_loss,
          stores[k]->parameters(),
          keep);
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gradient.size(); ++i)
        result.emplace(std::to_string(k) + "/" + stores[k]->names()[i], gradient[i]);
    }
    return result;
  };
  auto restore = [](const std::vector<n::ParameterStore*>& owners, const std::string& path) {
    auto arrays = n::load_npz(path);
    Require(arrays.size() == 32, "complete32-leaf checkpoint");
    for (const auto& [key, value] : arrays) {
      Require(
          key.size() > 2 && key[0] >= '0' && key[0] <= '3' && key[1] == '/',
          "known checkpoint prefix");
      auto& p = *owners[key[0] - '0'];
      Require(
          p.contains(key.substr(2)) && p.at(key.substr(2)).shape() == value.shape(),
          "known matching checkpoint tensor");
      p.set(key.substr(2), value);
    }
  };
  n::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind    = n::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  config.beta1   = .5;
  config.beta2   = .999;
  config.epsilon = 1e-8;
  std::vector<std::unique_ptr<n::Optimizer>> optimizers;
  for (auto* p : stores)
    optimizers.push_back(std::make_unique<n::Optimizer>(*p, .0002, config));
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root / "phases");

  if (!init.empty())
    restore(stores, init);
  Require(
      stores[0]->count() == 1390 && stores[1]->count() == 1390 && stores[2]->count() == 661 &&
          stores[3]->count() == 661,
      "4102 params");
  std::size_t tensors = 0;
  for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k)
    tensors += stores[k]->size();
  Require(tensors == 32, "32 tensors");
  SaveArrays((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), snapshot());
  SaveArrays((root / "initial_outputs.npz").string(), evaluate(domains[2].a, domains[2].b));
  nn::BatchOrder order_a(500, 32, 6233), order_b(500, 32, 6247);
  int            steps                   = 0;
  double         wrong_sequential_effect = 0;
  Tensor         first_a, first_b;
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\tg_loss\td_a_loss\td_b_loss\tcycle_loss_a\tcycle_loss_b\tidentity_loss_"
             "a\tidentity_loss_b\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\ta_row\tb_row\ta_source_id\tb_source_id\n";
  const auto ids_a   = nn::cast(domains[0].ids_a, nn::DType::Int64).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto ids_b   = nn::cast(domains[0].ids_b, nn::DType::Int64).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    order_a.begin_epoch();
    order_b.begin_epoch();
    for (;;) {
      const auto rows_a = order_a.next(), rows_b = order_b.next();
      Require(rows_a.size() == rows_b.size(), "equal domain batch sizes but independent orders");
      if (rows_a.empty())
        break;
      const Tensor a = Rows(domains[0].a, rows_a), b = Rows(domains[0].b, rows_b);
      if (!steps) {
        first_a = a, first_b = b;
        SaveArrays((root / "probe-first-input.npz").string(), {{"a", a}, {"b", b}});
        SaveArrays((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), evaluate(a, b));
      }
      for (int group : {2, 3}) {
        const auto captured = capture({group}, a, b);
        const auto phase    = "batch" + std::to_string(steps) + "-d" + std::to_string(group);
        SaveArrays((root / "phases" / (phase + "-gradient.npz")).string(), captured);
        const auto          before = snapshot();
        std::vector<Tensor> ordered;
        for (const auto& name : stores[group]->names())
          ordered.push_back(captured.at(std::to_string(group) + "/" + name));
        optimizers[group]->step(ordered);
        SaveArrays((root / "phases" / (phase + "-after.npz")).string(), snapshot());
        RequireOnlyOwnersChanged(
            before,
            snapshot(),
            {std::to_string(group) + "/"},
            "D step changes ONLY its own critic",
            false);
      }
      // Fresh forward through BOTH updated critics; capture BOTH G vectors before either write.
      const auto joint = capture({0, 1}, a, b);
      SaveArrays(
          (root / "phases" / ("batch" + std::to_string(steps) + "-g-gradient.npz")).string(),
          joint);
      for (int group : {0, 1}) {
        const auto          before = snapshot();
        std::vector<Tensor> ordered;
        for (const auto& name : stores[group]->names())
          ordered.push_back(joint.at(std::to_string(group) + "/" + name));
        optimizers[group]->step(ordered);
        SaveArrays(
            (root / "phases" /
             ("batch" + std::to_string(steps) + "-g" + std::to_string(group) + "-after.npz"))
                .string(),
            snapshot());
        RequireOnlyOwnersChanged(
            before,
            snapshot(),
            {std::to_string(group) + "/"},
            "captured G step changes ONLY own group",
            false);
        if (!steps && group == 0) {
          auto wrong = capture({1}, a, b);
          SaveArrays((root / "probe-wrong-sequential-gradient.npz").string(), wrong);
          for (const auto& [key, value] : wrong)
            wrong_sequential_effect =
                std::max(wrong_sequential_effect, MaxAbsDiff(value, joint.at(key)));
        }
      }
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i < rows_a.size(); ++i)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << steps << '\t' << rows_a[i] << '\t' << rows_b[i] << '\t'
                << ids_a[rows_a[i]] << '\t' << ids_b[rows_b[i]] << '\n';
      ++steps;
    }
    SaveArrays((root / ("probe-epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(), snapshot());
    SaveArrays(
        (root / ("probe-epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "-test.npz")).string(),
        evaluate(domains[2].a, domains[2].b));
    const auto v = evaluate(domains[1].a, domains[1].b);
    SaveArrays((root / ("probe-epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "-validation.npz")).string(), v);
    history << epoch;
    for (auto key :
         {"g_loss",
          "d_a_loss",
          "d_b_loss",
          "cycle_loss_a",
          "cycle_loss_b",
          "identity_loss_a",
          "identity_loss_b"})
      history << '\t' << Value(v, key);
    history << '\n';
    std::cout << "epoch " << epoch << ": G=" << Value(v, "g_loss")
              << ", cycle A/B=" << Value(v, "cycle_loss_a") << "/" << Value(v, "cycle_loss_b")
              << ", D A/B=" << Value(v, "d_a_loss") << "/" << Value(v, "d_b_loss") << std::endl;
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();
  Require(
      wrong_sequential_effect > 1e-8, "coupled G gradients MUST be captured before either write");

  const auto checkpoint = (root / "final.npz").string();
  for (auto& optimizer : optimizers)
    Require(optimizer->iterations() == 48, "four independent48-step counters");
  SaveArrays(checkpoint, snapshot());
  SaveArrays((root / "final_gradients.npz").string(), capture({0, 1, 2, 3}, first_a, first_b));
  std::vector<std::unique_ptr<n::ParameterStore>> restored;
  std::vector<n::ParameterStore*>                 restored_stores;
  for (int seed = 1; seed <= 4; ++seed) {
    restored.push_back(std::make_unique<n::ParameterStore>(seed));
    restored_stores.push_back(restored.back().get());
  }
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    auto           zero = n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1});
    m::Pix2PixGenerate(*restored_stores[0], zero);
    m::Pix2PixGenerate(*restored_stores[1], zero);
    m::CycleGanDiscriminate(*restored_stores[2], zero);
    m::CycleGanDiscriminate(*restored_stores[3], zero);
  }
  restore(restored_stores, checkpoint);
  auto restored_arrays = [&]() {
    Arrays a;
    for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k)
      for (const auto& name : restored_stores[k]->names())
        a.emplace(std::to_string(k) + "/" + name, restored_stores[k]->at(name).detach().clone());
    return a;
  };
  auto restored_evaluate = [&](const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    return Fields(
        m::CycleGan(
            *restored_stores[0],
            *restored_stores[1],
            *restored_stores[2],
            *restored_stores[3],
            a,
            b));
  };
  auto translate = [&](bool direction, const Tensor& image) {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    return m::Pix2PixGenerate(*restored_stores[direction ? 0 : 1], image).image;
  };
  Require(Equal(snapshot(), restored_arrays()), "all four groups restore exact");
  const auto   before = restored_arrays();
  const auto   output = restored_evaluate(domains[2].a, domains[2].b);
  const Tensor ab = translate(true, domains[2].a), ba = translate(false, domains[2].b);
  Require(
      Equal(ab, output.at("fake_b")) && Equal(ba, output.at("fake_a")),
      "SOURCE ONLY both translations without opposite domain images");
  double parity = 0;
  for (bool direction : {true, false})
    parity = std::max(
        parity,
        MaxAbsDiff(
            translate(direction, Rows(direction ? domains[2].a : domains[2].b, {0})),
            Rows(direction ? ab : ba, {0})));
  Require(parity < 2e-6, "both G single batch parity");
  Require(Equal(before, restored_arrays()), "immutable all four groups");
  SaveArrays((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  const Tensor true_b = m::RotateInvertGrayscale(domains[2].a), true_a = domains[2].original_b;
  SaveArrays(
      (root / "diagnostic_known_mapping.npz").string(),
      {{"a_to_b_target", true_b}, {"b_to_a_target", true_a}});
  auto mse = [](const Tensor& x, const Tensor& y) {
    return nn::mean(nn::square(nn::cast(x, nn::DType::Float64) - nn::cast(y, nn::DType::Float64)))
        .item();
  };
  const double mse_ab = mse(ab, true_b), mse_ba = mse(ba, true_a);
  for (bool direction : {true, false}) {
    std::vector<Tensor> rows;
    for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
      rows.push_back(Rows(direction ? domains[2].a : domains[2].b, {i}));
      rows.push_back(Rows(direction ? ab : ba, {i}));
      rows.push_back(Rows(output.at(direction ? "cycle_a" : "cycle_b"), {i}));
      rows.push_back(Rows(direction ? true_b : true_a, {i}));
    }
    const Tensor      gallery = nn::reshape(nn::concat(rows, 0), {40, 784});
    const std::string name    = direction ? "a_to_b" : "b_to_a";
    SaveArrays((root / (name + "_gallery.npz")).string(), {{"images", gallery}});
    Mosaic(root / (name + ".png"), gallery, 4);
  }
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":4102,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"steps_per_group\":" << steps
       << ",\"optimizer_updates\":" << 4 * steps << ",\"selected_epoch_fixed_final\":" << epochs
       << ",\"wrong_sequential_generator_gradient_max_difference\":" << wrong_sequential_effect
       << ",\"diagnostic_mapping_a_to_b_mse\":" << mse_ab
       << ",\"diagnostic_mapping_b_to_a_mse\":" << mse_ba
       << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity;
  for (auto key :
       {"g_loss",
        "d_a_loss",
        "d_b_loss",
        "cycle_loss_a",
        "cycle_loss_b",
        "identity_loss_a",
        "identity_loss_b"})
    meta << ",\"test_" << key << "\":" << Value(output, key);
  meta << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete CycleGAN records");
  meta.close();
  history.close();
  batches.close();
  std::cout << "fixed final=" << epochs
            << ", joint G snapshot wrong sequential difference=" << wrong_sequential_effect
            << ", mapping MSE=" << mse_ab << "/" << mse_ba
            << "; unpaired/joint grad/restore/source only/immutable PASS (training " << seconds
            << " s)\nArtifacts: " << root.string() << "\nAll cycle_gan checks passed.\n";
  std::ifstream file(root / "history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(file, header);
  std::vector<double> plot_epochs, ca, cb, ia, ib;
  double              ep, gl, dal, dbl, cal, cbl, ial, ibl;
  while (file >> ep >> gl >> dal >> dbl >> cal >> cbl >> ial >> ibl) {
    plot_epochs.push_back(ep);
    ca.push_back(cal);
    cb.push_back(cbl);
    ia.push_back(ial);
    ib.push_back(ibl);
  }
  auto learning = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  learning.y_limits(0, .9)
      .lines(plot_epochs, ca, "Cycle A", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(plot_epochs, ca, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .lines(plot_epochs, cb, "Cycle B", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(plot_epochs, cb, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .lines(plot_epochs, ia, "Identity A", {16, 145, 74}, 2)
      .points(plot_epochs, ia, "", {16, 145, 74}, 4)
      .lines(plot_epochs, ib, "Identity B", {147, 51, 234}, 2)
      .points(plot_epochs, ib, "", {147, 51, 234}, 4)
      .x_label("Completed epoch; fixed final3 without early stopping")
      .y_label("Validation mean absolute pixel error, unit range")
      .title("Three epochs leave large cycle and identity errors")
      .save_svg("build/cycle_learning.svg");
}
